Task: Update the guidance based on entries classified as triage failures or successes.

The output MUST have exactly two sections:

## Symptom Areas
Each item is a broad symptom area the triage agent should check, with a brief description
of what to look for. Examples:
- Service-to-pod port mapping: compare every Service's targetPort against its pods' containerPort.
- Pod health: pods not in Running/Completed state.

## Anomaly Hints
Specific anomaly patterns worth flagging (non-exhaustive — the agent should still flag
anything that looks wrong). Examples:
- Services whose selector labels don't match any pod.
- ConfigMaps injecting scripts or overriding entrypoints.

When to add:
- The classification shows the triage missed a resource type or anomaly pattern that
  turned out to be the root cause.
- A new anomaly shape was discovered that the triage should catch in future problems.

When to remove or refine:
- An area or hint consistently produces benign noise that distracts the agent.
- Evidence contradicts an existing item.
- Two items say essentially the same thing — merge them.

Rules:
- Keep both sections short and high-signal. Do NOT blindly append every new observation —
  only add items that would have changed the outcome if the agent had known them.
  Prefer generalizing an existing item over adding a near-duplicate.
- Maximum 10 symptom areas, maximum 15 anomaly hints.
- Each item must be generic (no app-specific names or values).
- Preserve items that were not implicated — do not remove working guidance.
- Output only the two sections with their items, no preamble or commentary.
